y who study social questions\nwith computational methods. We meet weekly for hands-on sessions, and we build\nthings together — models, datasets, and small simulations anyone can run.\n:::\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.content-body}\n\n::: {.prose}\n::: {.eyebrow}\nWhat we do\n:::\n\n## Social questions, computational instruments\n\nThe society brings together people from political science, sociology, economics,\nhistory, and computer engineering. Our shared premise is that many social questions\nturn on processes we cannot observe directly — how opinions spread, how ties form,\nhow what people say diverges from what they believe. Computational methods let us\nstate those processes precisely and test them against data.\n\nSessions are informal and hands-on. Someone brings a problem or a paper, we work\nthrough the code together, and everyone leaves with something they can run. No\nprior programming experience is required to attend — several of our current members\nstarted with none.\n:::\n\n::: {.eyebrow}\nMethods\n:::\n\n::: {.methods}\n\n::: {.method}\n### Agent-based modeling\nBuilding populations of interacting agents to see which macro patterns follow from\nwhich micro rules. We work mainly in NetLogo and Python.\n:::\n\n::: {.method}\n### Network analysis\nTreating relationships as data: alliance networks, retweet networks, co-authorship.\nDescriptive statistics through to ERGMs and community detection.\n:::\n\n::: {.method}\n### Text as data\nTurning documents, speeches, and social media into measurable quantities, with\nparticular attention to Turkish-language NLP.\n:::\n\n::: {.method}\n### Machine learning\nPrediction and classification applied to social data, alongside the harder question\nof when prediction is and is not the right tool.\n:::\n\n:::\n\n::: {.prose}\n::: {.eyebrow}\nJoining\n:::\n\n## Come to a session\n\nWe meet weekly during term at the Department of Political Science and International\nRelations. Meetings are open — no membership form, no prerequisite. Bring a laptop\nif you have one.\n\nWrite to us at the address on the [contact page](contact.qmd) and we will add you to\nthe mailing list for meeting times and readings.\n:::\n\n:::\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":true,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","toc":false,"include-in-header":["head.html"],"email-obfuscation":"javascript","output-file":"index.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of contents","toc-title-website":"On this page","related-formats-title":"Other Formats","related-notebooks-title":"Notebooks","source-notebooks-prefix":"Source","other-links-title":"Other Links","code-links-title":"Code Links","launch-dev-container-title":"Launch Dev Container","launch-binder-title":"L